SHAMSU — P0: unredacted prompts on disk. chat-logs/ removed.
============================================================
2026-08-21 · branch small-shamsu-new


THE LEAK, PROVEN BEFORE ANYTHING WAS CHANGED
--------------------------------------------
One scripted turn whose prompt and reply both contained
`api_key=sk-livesecret9876`, then a search of EVERY file under `.shamsu/`.
Deliberately not a check of files we remembered to name - that is how the
second leak below stayed hidden.

    searching every file under .../leakcheck/.shamsu for 'sk-livesecret9876'

      LEAKED  .shamsu\chat-logs\20260821-124041-6dd3--untitled-session.md
      LEAKED  .shamsu\logs\20260821-124041-6dd3\model-transcript.csv

    log-detailed.md: redacted=True secret_present=False

TWO leaks, not one.

1. `shamsu/agents/simple_log.py` -> `.shamsu/chat-logs/<session>.md`
   Zero calls to `redact` anywhere in the module. It wrote the exact prompt
   (system message included) and the raw reply for every turn of every
   session, at every log level. The one path in the project that put model
   text on disk without going through the shared secret-pattern list.

2. `ActionLedger._append_friendly_csv_row` -> `.shamsu/logs/<id>/model-transcript.csv`
   NOT known before this work. The markdown twin of the same table goes
   through `_markdown_cell`, which calls `redact_text`; the CSV writer wrote
   the row dict straight out. Same row, same data, and the `.md` said
   `[REDACTED]` while the `.csv` beside it held the key in clear text:

     .md   | ... | [model_0000.response.txt](...)<br>I will use [REDACTED] for that. |
     .csv  | ... | [model_0000.response.txt](...)<br>I will use api_key=sk-livesecret9876 for that.

   Fixed by redacting every field on the way out, exactly as the markdown
   writer has always done. One line.


WHAT WAS REMOVED
----------------
`shamsu/agents/simple_log.py` (deleted), and its 20 call sites in
`shamsu/agents/simple_chat.py`:

    the import, the `turn_log` attribute, construction + open_turn,
    log_call, log_response, log_error, log_tool_result (x5),
    close_turn (x4)

That left `log_turns` and `SHAMSU_NO_CHAT_LOG` controlling nothing, so both
went too - a constructor flag named "log turns" that silently does not is worse
than no flag. Four test call sites updated.


WHAT MOVED, SO NOTHING WAS LOST
-------------------------------
`chat-logs/` kept the full prompt at EVERY level. `log-detailed.md` kept it
only at `verbose`. Deleting the leak would therefore have taken the record with
it, so `turnlog.append_model_call` no longer gates on verbosity.

The prompt is now written at both levels, through the redactor, and the
overflow rule keeps a large one out of the document body - live, a 4.7k prompt
spilled to `sessions/<id>/attachments/turn_...-0002-prompt.txt`.

The line between the two levels moved twice today, and now sits at: `essential`
keeps the record (prompt, response, reasoning); `verbose` adds the context
pack, which is the largest payload a turn produces and the one thing genuinely
reconstructable from elsewhere.


THE WARNING
-----------
`turnlog.legacy_chat_logs(workspace)` / `legacy_chat_logs_warning(workspace)`,
shown once at startup by `_print_startup_banner`:

    ┌─ Unredacted logs ────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ Old chat logs found: <workspace>\.shamsu\chat-logs               │
    │ These 3 files were written before 2026-08-21 by a logger that did │
    │ NOT redact secrets, so any API key or password mentioned in a     │
    │ prompt is in them in clear text. Nothing writes there any more -  │
    │ the readable log now lives in .shamsu/sessions/<id>/ and is       │
    │ redacted. Delete the folder when you no longer need the history.  │
    └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

At startup rather than per turn: it is a fact about the workspace, not about
anything the agent is doing, and a line repeated after every turn is a line
nobody reads. An EMPTY leftover folder is not a leak and gets no panel.

SHAMSU does not delete the folder. The files may be the only record of sessions
someone still wants, and silently removing a user's logs to fix our bug is not
ours to decide. There is a test asserting the warning leaves the files alone.


VERIFICATION
------------
Same probe, after:

    searching every file under .../leakfinal/.shamsu for 'sk-livesecret9876'

      (nothing leaked)

    log-detailed.md: redacted=True secret_present=False
                     has the prompt sent? True

Every file the session produced, and `chat-logs/` is not among them:

    .shamsu/README.md
    .shamsu/logs/<id>/agent-development-log.jsonl
    .shamsu/logs/<id>/model-transcript.{csv,md}
    .shamsu/logs/<id>/model-transcript/model_0000.{prompt,response}.txt
    .shamsu/runs/<run>/.evidence/{events,decisions,tool-calls,model-calls}.jsonl
    .shamsu/runs/<run>/.evidence/attachments/mutations.jsonl
    .shamsu/sessions/<id>/log-summary.md
    .shamsu/sessions/<id>/log-detailed.md
    .shamsu/sessions/<id>/attachments/turn_...-prompt.txt
    .shamsu/sessions/<id>/{session,owner}.json


TESTS
-----
Nine tests were deleted with the module. The properties they guaranteed that
still matter were ported to the redacted log rather than dropped:

    test_no_secret_in_the_prompt_reaches_any_file_on_disk
        the headline, asserted over the WHOLE tree rather than a named file -
        a test that only checked the files we remembered would have missed
        both of the leaks above.
    test_the_prompt_as_sent_is_kept_at_every_level
        the system prompt and the raw response are visible, at essential.
    test_a_pydantic_response_is_not_recorded_as_empty
        the client returns a ChatResponse, not a dict; reading it with .get()
        once logged every response as empty. Thinking captured too.
    test_a_whole_tool_result_survives_rather_than_being_clipped
        chat-logs set its truncation limit to zero on purpose. The overflow
        rule replaces that: the payload leaves the document and keeps every
        byte in attachments/.
    test_a_broken_log_never_breaks_the_turn
    test_the_legacy_chat_logs_directory_is_no_longer_written
    test_a_workspace_with_old_chat_logs_is_warned
    test_a_clean_workspace_is_not_warned
    test_the_warning_never_deletes_anything
    test_the_startup_banner_shows_the_warning

    tests/test_trace_output.py   47 -> 57
    tests/test_simple_chat.py    9 removed with the module
